WEBVTT

01:29.980 --> 01:33.480
<b>Primary</b>

01:29.980 --> 01:33.480
<b></b>Examinee Number

01:29.980 --> 01:33.480
<b></b>Name

01:29.980 --> 01:33.480
<b>Kobato Jogoro</b>

01:30.520 --> 01:33.480
<b>Episode 1: Sheep Costume</b>

01:44.500 --> 01:47.000
<b></b>Where are you right now?

01:44.500 --> 01:47.000
<b></b>Where are you right now?

02:05.940 --> 02:07.090
Me, too.

02:08.600 --> 02:11.120
Kobato-kun, you made it in, right?

02:12.050 --> 02:13.310
I see.

02:13.310 --> 02:15.430
So you also made it, Osanai-san.

02:15.430 --> 02:16.420
That's great.

02:16.420 --> 02:16.980
Yeah.

02:18.730 --> 02:19.750
I'll be seeing you.

02:21.240 --> 02:23.430
It's cold out here. I'm heading home.

02:23.950 --> 02:27.010
Why don't we go get some 
sweets to celebrate?

02:27.010 --> 02:27.900
Sounds good.

02:30.850 --> 02:32.800
Don't move, Kobato-kun!

02:35.720 --> 02:39.400
Wasn't she in your class?

02:41.140 --> 02:42.340
I see.

02:43.910 --> 02:46.230
She might not have been accepted.

02:47.100 --> 02:49.040
I'm failing to be an ordinary person, huh?

02:49.040 --> 02:50.760
You. Over there.

02:52.620 --> 02:54.770
Well, look who it is.

02:55.120 --> 02:56.970
That's a rude welcome.

02:57.380 --> 02:59.190
It's been a long time, Kengo.

03:00.280 --> 03:09.870
<b>Funato High School Map</b>

03:00.660 --> 03:03.120
You applied for Funato 
High School, too, huh?

03:03.120 --> 03:04.910
Yeah. I did.

03:05.270 --> 03:06.360
I see.

03:06.360 --> 03:08.150
We're in the same school again.

03:08.150 --> 03:09.880
I never said I got accepted.

03:10.870 --> 03:14.370
I'd never expect you to 
botch a cerebral task.

03:18.500 --> 03:21.720
Osanai-san, he's a bit brutish, 
but you don't need to be afraid.

03:22.280 --> 03:24.110
Who are you calling brutish?

03:24.110 --> 03:25.230
Sorry.

03:25.230 --> 03:26.670
I guess I should say "scary."

03:27.190 --> 03:29.110
This is Dojima Kengo.

03:29.110 --> 03:30.850
We were in the same elementary school.

03:33.970 --> 03:35.940
This is Osanai-san.

03:35.940 --> 03:37.770
We were in the same middle school.

03:37.770 --> 03:39.140
We're friends.

03:39.140 --> 03:40.960
Hello, Osanai-san.

03:41.440 --> 03:44.890
You must be pretty tough to 
be friends with Jogoro.

03:51.480 --> 03:52.420
Like it?

03:52.700 --> 03:53.770
Yeah.

03:54.650 --> 03:56.180
It's good.

03:56.850 --> 04:01.270
Actually, I have one more thing 
to look forward to this month.

04:01.270 --> 04:02.410
Oh?

04:04.120 --> 04:05.920
Strawberry tarts.

04:06.750 --> 04:10.510
There's a shop that sells really nice 
strawberry tarts exclusively in the spring.

04:10.510 --> 04:11.660
Yeah?

04:16.710 --> 04:22.040
It's just... I'm sure you know already, 
but I don't have much of a sweet tooth.

04:23.450 --> 04:27.920
After all, there's a sweet smell 
in my house all the time.

04:29.030 --> 04:30.750
I'm jealous.

04:30.750 --> 04:32.570
It's a bit much when it's every day.

04:33.960 --> 04:38.800
The Japanese confectioneries your parents 
sell aren't too sweet. They're refined.

04:39.820 --> 04:44.570
It's a beautiful shop, 
but it's not really my type.

04:45.030 --> 04:46.600
My type is...

04:46.600 --> 04:49.060
First and foremost, 
you prefer western snacks

04:49.060 --> 04:54.420
that are very sweet and have distinct 
flavors such as butter and brandy.

04:54.800 --> 05:00.240
But you don't like intense flavors. 
You're looking for a perfect balance.

05:08.610 --> 05:10.920
By the way, Kobato-kun...

05:10.920 --> 05:13.080
What's Dojima-kun like?

05:13.730 --> 05:15.000
Are you curious?

05:19.600 --> 05:23.850
I worry that he's going to impose on you.

05:24.750 --> 05:28.750
I shouldn't say this about someone 
I've only just met, but he's...

05:29.880 --> 05:31.040
You're right.

05:31.040 --> 05:33.020
He can be pretty meddlesome.

05:33.020 --> 05:35.660
He's very much not an ordinary person.

05:36.550 --> 05:40.140
"An ordinary person must never stand out."

05:40.140 --> 05:44.000
"They must spend every day in peace 
and do everything possible

05:44.000 --> 05:46.880
to avoid anything that interferes with that."

05:49.030 --> 05:50.920
Don't worry, though.

05:51.410 --> 05:53.650
Kengo's a good guy.

05:55.710 --> 05:58.160
That makes me even more worried.

06:15.190 --> 06:16.440
Strawberry tarts?

06:16.780 --> 06:19.670
Yeah. The spring exclusive I was talking about.

06:19.670 --> 06:22.770
A shop called Alice makes them.
They have lots of strawberries.

06:22.770 --> 06:25.200
Wow, that sounds exciting.

06:25.200 --> 06:26.450
The sale ends today.

06:26.860 --> 06:29.450
Could you come with me?

06:31.360 --> 06:35.290
I'm assuming it's one per customer.

06:35.290 --> 06:38.660
Yeah. They're going to sell out 
if we don't get there quick.

06:38.660 --> 06:42.660
I went around 4:30 PM last year, 
and they only had one left.

06:45.620 --> 06:46.970
How far is it from here?

06:47.720 --> 06:49.730
About twenty minutes by foot?

06:49.730 --> 06:51.320
I think we'll make it.

06:54.570 --> 06:55.400
Kengo.

06:57.250 --> 06:59.430
Yeah, I was on my way home.

07:00.460 --> 07:02.610
You need a hand? For how long?

07:04.560 --> 07:06.330
Half an hour?

07:10.170 --> 07:14.110
If they sell out, I won't 
get any until next spring.

07:14.110 --> 07:15.210
But...

07:15.210 --> 07:16.260
But?

07:16.260 --> 07:21.170
"Do not turn down a request from an 
acquaintance, lest you cause a disturbance."

07:21.170 --> 07:22.660
That is the...

07:23.750 --> 07:25.010
I'll wait.

07:29.930 --> 07:31.960
There's something I want you to find.

07:32.320 --> 07:33.340
A pochette.

07:33.720 --> 07:34.900
A pochette?

07:35.740 --> 07:37.130
It belongs to her.

07:37.130 --> 07:38.100
It was stolen.

07:38.590 --> 07:41.240
Yoshiguchi, was there 
anything of value inside?

07:41.650 --> 07:43.310
No.

07:43.310 --> 07:45.860
Lip balm, ballpoint pens,

07:45.860 --> 07:48.940
scissors, and my planner, I think.

07:49.460 --> 07:52.330
It doesn't sound like the kind 
of thing that'd get stolen.

07:52.910 --> 07:55.500
It may also have been hidden.

07:55.840 --> 07:59.350
We've decided to check around the campus.

08:01.240 --> 08:03.930
How would you describe the 
pochette we're looking for?

08:04.680 --> 08:09.000
It's about this big, deep red in color.

08:09.000 --> 08:11.880
It has a thin shoulder strap 
and a white lining.

08:11.880 --> 08:13.550
When did it go missing?

08:13.550 --> 08:16.760
I had it until we changed 
for gym class in sixth period.

08:16.760 --> 08:19.690
It was gone when I got back.

08:21.560 --> 08:24.270
It doesn't sound like you simply misplaced it.

08:24.710 --> 08:25.760
I didn't.

08:27.630 --> 08:28.770
Let's start.

08:28.770 --> 08:30.330
I'll check the first floor.

08:30.330 --> 08:32.750
Dude, don't go straight for the easiest task.

08:32.750 --> 08:35.140
We're taking time out of our 
busy schedule to help—

08:35.140 --> 08:36.720
I'll do the fourth floor, then.

08:36.720 --> 08:38.460
Shimomura, you take the third floor.

08:40.170 --> 08:41.740
Fine, I guess.

08:42.610 --> 08:45.790
Okay. Jogoro, please take the second floor.

08:49.920 --> 08:51.010
I'm counting on you.

08:55.590 --> 08:57.260
Yoshiguchi-san, was it?

08:57.670 --> 08:58.850
This is rough, huh?

08:59.460 --> 09:00.380
Yeah.

09:01.010 --> 09:06.910
Kengo... Dojima didn't pressure you 
into letting him look for it, did he?

09:08.150 --> 09:09.630
Nah.

09:09.630 --> 09:12.580
I appreciate him helping out,

09:13.110 --> 09:15.650
but he's been so eager about it

09:15.650 --> 09:22.240
that I worry it might look like 
I charmed these four guys into helping me.

09:23.140 --> 09:24.950
You don't owe us anything.

09:25.300 --> 09:27.250
Kengo's the one who asked us, after all.

09:27.860 --> 09:31.540
Could you try searching the 
places guys can't get into?

09:32.460 --> 09:33.330
Okay.

09:37.210 --> 09:38.960
A pochette.

09:40.370 --> 09:42.480
Nothing of monetary value.

09:43.270 --> 09:46.580
Was with her until gym class in sixth period.

09:48.850 --> 09:51.120
Gone when she got back.

09:53.490 --> 09:55.110
Stolen?

09:55.490 --> 09:56.910
Hidden?

09:57.650 --> 09:59.000
Or maybe...

10:09.100 --> 10:10.550
He's really trying.

10:11.750 --> 10:17.760
<b>Notes</b>

10:11.750 --> 10:17.760
<b>Buy spring exclusive strawberry tarts at Alice


\h\h(Ideally two)</b>

10:11.750 --> 10:17.760
<b>Then buy milk (500ml carton)</b>

10:11.750 --> 10:17.760
<b>Return home quickly</b>

10:11.750 --> 10:17.760
<b>Eat one strawberry tart after dinner</b>

10:17.760 --> 10:21.220
"Eat the other tomorrow morning."

10:25.650 --> 10:28.650
Wow, you used to play badminton, huh?

10:32.970 --> 10:34.600
<i>Oh, it's Jogoro.</i>

10:34.600 --> 10:35.670
<i>Where are you?</i>

10:35.670 --> 10:37.680
The second floor corridor.

10:37.680 --> 10:39.570
<i>Stay right there. Don't move.</i>

10:39.570 --> 10:40.840
<i>I'll come to you.</i>

10:43.720 --> 10:45.220
Takada, that idiot...

10:45.220 --> 10:47.320
He called and said he was done searching,

10:47.320 --> 10:49.510
so I suggested we regroup,

10:49.510 --> 10:52.620
but he hung up without confirming where.

10:52.620 --> 10:54.610
I call him back, and he doesn't pick up.

10:54.610 --> 10:56.920
And when I go to the spot
 I suggested, he isn't there.

10:56.920 --> 11:00.240
I ask him where he is, and he keeps moving
between the third and fourth floors.

11:00.240 --> 11:02.110
Sorry you had to deal with that.

11:02.810 --> 11:05.260
So, where's the other guy?

11:05.260 --> 11:07.500
Shimomura already went home.

11:07.500 --> 11:09.070
Right after we split up.

11:09.560 --> 11:10.580
Huh.

11:18.290 --> 11:20.040
Sorry, I should....

11:20.720 --> 11:21.830
Takada.

11:21.830 --> 11:23.890
Stay put, you moron. Got it?

11:24.700 --> 11:25.840
Now?

11:25.840 --> 11:27.710
The second floor corridor.

11:27.710 --> 11:28.820
Jogoro—

11:28.820 --> 11:30.360
Kobato and I have met up.

11:30.360 --> 11:31.340
You don't...

11:31.340 --> 11:33.990
What? Outside?

11:38.710 --> 11:40.540
He doesn't need to wave so hard.

11:41.120 --> 11:42.340
Don't you dare hang up.

11:43.920 --> 11:46.490
Come to the spot where we met up earlier.

11:46.490 --> 11:48.560
I'm done playing tag with you.

11:53.560 --> 11:55.350
Takada, that asshole...

11:55.350 --> 11:57.710
"That's my line," he says.

12:05.090 --> 12:07.860
Have any of you found any promising leads?

12:10.000 --> 12:13.090
If it doesn't turn up, 
we'll have to ask the police to—

12:13.090 --> 12:14.050
The police?!

12:14.470 --> 12:15.960
You need to chill.

12:15.960 --> 12:17.460
Something was stolen.

12:17.810 --> 12:19.630
This is theft.

12:19.630 --> 12:22.910
I've got no chill for anyone 
who'd steal a girl's things.

12:37.800 --> 12:40.950
Anyway, shall we call it a day?

12:40.950 --> 12:42.060
Yeah.

12:43.770 --> 12:44.800
Sorry.

12:45.320 --> 12:46.440
It's okay.

12:46.440 --> 12:47.900
Let's go.

12:47.900 --> 12:48.870
Okay.

12:48.870 --> 12:52.460
But there's something 
I want to ask you first.

12:52.460 --> 12:55.580
Will it be quick?

12:56.990 --> 12:58.590
That's the gist of it.

12:59.260 --> 13:04.030
My suspicion is that this case can be
 solved with one witness testimony.

13:04.770 --> 13:06.380
Witness?

13:09.510 --> 13:14.350
Why did Takada-kun go all the 
way outside just to wave at us?

13:16.970 --> 13:19.200
Because he wanted to?

13:19.200 --> 13:21.340
Because he wanted to wear his shoes?

13:21.340 --> 13:24.360
Or because he wanted to 
take off his indoor shoes?

13:25.070 --> 13:30.570
By going outside to wave, he was able 
to cover up his whereabouts until then.

13:49.880 --> 13:53.680
It takes a while for clothes to dry.

13:55.140 --> 13:56.770
<b></b>Calling

13:55.140 --> 13:56.770
<b></b>Dojima Kengo

13:56.770 --> 13:58.880
Right now? Third floor.

13:59.740 --> 14:00.890
I'm on the fourth floor now.

14:01.460 --> 14:03.280
North wing.

14:03.700 --> 14:05.780
So he waited for the right moment

14:06.490 --> 14:10.490
to set up the story that he got his 
tracksuit wet by going outside right then.

14:11.910 --> 14:17.500
And he waited by the staircase 
for that moment to come.

14:18.420 --> 14:22.800
The witness I'm talking about is someone 
who was watching at that time.

14:24.560 --> 14:25.560
I saw him.

14:26.090 --> 14:29.250
A brawny-looking guy in a tracksuit.

14:30.060 --> 14:31.590
It's settled, then.

14:32.250 --> 14:36.680
Kengo said the pochette 
was either stolen or hidden.

14:37.490 --> 14:42.940
But there's one other 
possibility I want to add:

14:42.940 --> 14:44.380
something was planted in it.

14:44.860 --> 14:45.930
Planted?

15:03.930 --> 15:05.720
Impressive as always, Kobato-kun.

15:08.000 --> 15:09.510
Pardon me.

15:10.590 --> 15:11.990
The thing that was planted...

15:13.720 --> 15:15.090
was probably this.

15:13.720 --> 15:15.100
<b></b>Yoshiguchi-san

15:15.220 --> 15:17.220
<b></b>Takada

15:15.820 --> 15:16.790
What could it be?

15:21.040 --> 15:22.000
Hey!

15:23.440 --> 15:26.940
What do you think you're doing, 
looking inside someone's bag?

15:29.850 --> 15:31.210
What's with <i>you</i>?

15:32.080 --> 15:33.600
I'm Osanai.

15:33.600 --> 15:35.620
I'm Kobato-kun's friend.

15:37.570 --> 15:38.570
Umm...

15:40.570 --> 15:43.870
If you come any closer,

15:43.870 --> 15:48.710
I'll run somewhere with more people 
and hand this over to Yoshiguchi-san.

15:58.770 --> 16:00.260
All right.

16:00.260 --> 16:01.720
I apologize.

16:13.210 --> 16:15.820
That's a love letter, isn't it?

16:17.090 --> 16:20.470
You didn't have the courage 
to hand it to her in person,

16:21.050 --> 16:23.390
so you put it in her pochette.

16:25.400 --> 16:29.340
But you realized that was a bad idea, 
so you tried to take it back.

16:30.850 --> 16:38.110
I don't think you're in any position to
criticize him for looking inside the pochette.

16:39.270 --> 16:41.030
You're right.

16:41.030 --> 16:43.200
I can't believe I did that.

16:43.200 --> 16:44.670
It was a lapse in judgment.

16:46.890 --> 16:48.900
I'm glad you understand.

16:50.770 --> 16:53.540
Well, we need to get going.

16:53.540 --> 16:56.020
You two get it, though, don't you?

16:56.420 --> 16:57.730
If you're dating...

16:59.040 --> 17:02.190
You must know how I felt 
when I put the letter in there.

17:15.560 --> 17:19.300
Takada-kun was out of everyone's sight.

17:19.300 --> 17:22.210
I wonder why he didn't take the letter out.

17:22.670 --> 17:24.840
I'm just guessing now, but...

17:39.410 --> 17:40.780
<b></b>Calling

17:39.410 --> 17:40.780
<b></b>Dojima Kengo

17:54.630 --> 17:56.300
I think Takada-kun will

17:56.300 --> 17:59.870
put the pochette back in Yoshiguchi-san's
locker by the end of the day.

18:00.730 --> 18:05.400
That way, Yoshiguchi-san 
won't report the incident.

18:10.250 --> 18:11.390
This is bad.

18:13.020 --> 18:15.010
They might have already sold out.

18:16.810 --> 18:18.320
This way should be faster.

18:20.170 --> 18:22.120
If the police catch us, though,

18:22.120 --> 18:24.340
strawberry tarts will be 
the least of our worries.

18:30.760 --> 18:33.250
Hey, about what he said earlier...

18:34.100 --> 18:37.030
That we'd understand if we were dating.

18:38.640 --> 18:41.060
That's not a situation I'll ever be in.

18:42.830 --> 18:44.600
Me neither.

18:44.890 --> 18:47.600
You ended up solving the mystery, Kobato-kun.

18:47.940 --> 18:50.710
No, that was just...

19:02.020 --> 19:03.110
It's fine.

19:04.510 --> 19:08.620
If you can't stop, 
you can use me as an excuse.

19:09.570 --> 19:11.680
You don't need to hold back.

19:15.120 --> 19:16.130
Of course.

19:16.130 --> 19:18.630
We'd promised that was 
what we'd do for each other.

19:21.130 --> 19:24.930
That's how the two of us 
create our moments of peace...

19:24.930 --> 19:29.140
...and make a giant leap towards 
becoming completely ordinary.

19:53.500 --> 19:56.180
I'd like a spring exclusive strawberry tart.

19:58.370 --> 19:59.730
Right.

19:59.730 --> 20:01.430
One for me, too.

20:02.040 --> 20:03.430
Lucky you.

20:03.430 --> 20:05.090
These are the last two.

20:07.930 --> 20:10.430
<b>Spring Sweets Fair</b>

20:12.700 --> 20:14.060
Let's go.

20:14.060 --> 20:17.220
Sorry, I actually can't.

20:17.220 --> 20:19.440
What do you mean, you can't?

20:19.440 --> 20:21.020
I told you to make time.

20:21.460 --> 20:23.560
No, it's not that I don't have time.

20:23.990 --> 20:25.650
I just can't get there.

20:25.650 --> 20:27.150
What about the bike?

20:27.150 --> 20:29.010
You went home to get it, didn't you?

20:29.010 --> 20:30.200
It got stolen.

20:30.560 --> 20:34.700
Ozaki-san, did you hear that? 
Sakagami says his bike got stolen.

20:36.270 --> 20:38.140
Figure it out.

20:38.600 --> 20:40.030
You know where we're going.

20:40.450 --> 20:41.720
Be there in ten minutes.

20:59.500 --> 21:01.280
Tarts, tarts, tarts...

21:10.590 --> 21:11.690
Thief!
